(* CALIBRATION 1 of 2 — this formula MUST evaluate to TRUE.

   Nothing else in this directory may be believed until both calibration
   formulas return the answers stated at the top of their files.

   WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
   --------------------
   In MCL a double-quoted action is a LITERAL string, not a regular
   expression. "SUBMISSION_STATUS.*" therefore matches a label whose text ends
   in a full stop and an asterisk -- i.e. nothing at all -- and every formula
   written that way comes back FALSE. During this case study that produced two
   confidently reported findings ("the stale interleaving is unreachable",
   "the pairing is unenforced") which were both artefacts of the notation.
   Both reversed once the formulas were written properly.

   A formula that returns FALSE because it matched nothing is
   indistinguishable, in the output, from a formula that returns FALSE because
   the property genuinely fails. The only defence is to calibrate: prove the
   label text you are using DOES match something before drawing any conclusion
   from its absence.

   Labels here are exact strings taken from the generated test cases, which are
   projections of this same composed model, so they are known to occur.

   Expected: TRUE
*)
< true* . "SAVE_SUBMISSION !CRS_0 !ASN_0 !PLACEHOLDER" > true
